[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093050254,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093116417,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093123102,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093128191,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093132474,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093136493,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093140203,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093143814,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093147694,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093150131,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093152543,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.09315583,"data":"| Kaggle CPU kernel (the default) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer whose widest density matrix stays below `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS`, and the CI gate shards (`kaggle_run.py shards`) | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093164721,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU, `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4`) | simulations whose widest density matrix reaches `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS` | IBM jobs; narrow replays the CPU runs faster |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093169245,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093173873,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (`TpuV5E8`, `TpuV6E8`) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend. Batch pushes requesting either ID ran on 4-core CPU machines without libtpu, so this account reaches no TPU through the CLI | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093178343,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093182201,"data":"| IBM Heron (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 15 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.09318604,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093190481,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB; guide in the untracked `docs/local/`) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, CPU replays, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093195232,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.09319883,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093202777,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093206405,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093210186,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093213961,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093217482,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093223148,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093227382,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093238987,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack. The kernel fetches the eight\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093243078,"data":"   pinned archives (sha256-checked), installs them through the PKGBUILD\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093247018,"data":"   recipes in `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`, runs `--extract`, and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093251172,"data":"   stops with exit code 3 unless the regenerated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093255106,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json` equals the retained bytes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093257611,"data":"   The build host passes the same test against its Arch packages, so a run\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093260511,"data":"   that reaches its entry used the same algebra code as the host.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093264622,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093268655,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093272512,"data":"4. The entry's stdout, stderr, exit code and changed files.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093276592,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093279997,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093283854,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.09328765,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093291009,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093294974,"data":"| qiskit | 2.5.2 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093298754,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093302937,"data":"| qiskit-ibm-runtime | 0.50.0 (fake backends such as FakeFez; no account or credential) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093306893,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093311276,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093315302,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI (Cayley-Calculator runtime) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093319331,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093323264,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093327523,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093331121,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093334832,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093338415,"data":"- A kernel is private, has internet enabled (and a GPU when one is\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093342184,"data":"  requested), and holds no IBM credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093346383,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093349262,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE`, which the kernel sets to its\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093351707,"data":"  machine's device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093355178,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093358806,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.09336744,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093372152,"data":"- The push selects hardware with `--accelerator`; `environment.json`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.09337631,"data":"  records what actually ran.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093379978,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape, the qubit size guide and the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.09338366,"data":"  captured Kaggle documentation are in `docs/notes/kaggle/`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":20.093387198,"data":"\n"}
